    "result": "Done! I've fixed the floating-point precision bug in three functions across two files:\n\n**src/money.js:**\n- `parseEuros()` - converts typed amounts like \"39.95\" to cents\n- `cellCents()` - converts spreadsheet amounts to cents\n\n**src/locale.js:**\n- `decimalCommaToCents()` - converts European-style amounts like \"12,99\" to cents\n\nThe issue was that when multiplying decimal values by 100 to convert to cents, JavaScript's floating-point arithmetic was introducing tiny errors (e.g., 39.95 \u00d7 100 = 3995.0000000000005). I added `Math.round()` to ensure all results are exact whole numbers. Now your Gym membership at 39.95 will work perfectly alongside Netflix and Spotify!\n\nAll 51 tests pass with this fix. When you're ready, the changes are staged and waiting for a `git commit`.",
